[15 Regression] Wrong code at -O1 -fipa-pta
$ cat bug.c
int
is_valid_domain_name (const char *string)
{
  const char *s;

  for (s=string; *s; s++)
    if (*s == '.')
      {
        if (string == s)
          return 0;
      }

  return !!*string;
}

int
main (void)
{
  static struct
  {
    const char *name;
    int valid;
  } testtbl[] =
    {
      { ".", 0 },
      { nullptr, 0 }
    };
  int idx;

  for (idx=0; testtbl[idx].name; idx++)
    {
      if (is_valid_domain_name (testtbl[idx].name) != testtbl[idx].valid)
        __builtin_abort ();
    }
}
$ cc bug.c -std=c23 -O1 -fipa-pta -flto
$ ./a.out
[1]    301695 IOT instruction (core dumped)  ./a.out

Removing any of -fipa-pta -flto can work around the issue.  The code is reduced from gnupg-2.4.7, it only fails at -O1 but the original gnupg code fails at -O2 and -O3 as well.

The output of GCC 14 is fine.
